course: dictionary
lesson: 6152
title: Meet the millipede
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A millipede is a small creature with a long body made of many segments, and most of those segments have two pairs of legs. It lives in damp soil and under leaf litter, and it eats dead plants.
explain: The name millipede means thousand feet, but most millipedes have far fewer than that. «Millipede means thousand feet, but most have fewer than 400 legs.» When a name sounds like a big number, check it against the facts.
explain: Millipedes are not insects, and they are not centipedes. «Millipedes have two pairs of legs on most body sections and centipedes have one pair, which is how you tell them apart.» Count the legs on each segment and you can tell which one you have found.
fact: A millipede has a long body made of many segments, with two pairs of legs on most of them.
fact: Millipedes live in damp soil and leaf litter, and they eat dead plants.
fact: When frightened, a millipede curls into a tight coil to protect itself.
fact: In 2020 scientists found a millipede with 1,306 legs in a deep drill hole in Australia, the first known with more than a thousand.
fact: Millipedes help break down dead leaves into soil, so they are important in nature.
exercise: «Millipedes are slow, eat dead plants, and curl into a tight coil to protect themselves.» What do millipedes eat? | Fish | Bread | *Dead plants | Live birds
exercise: Millipede means thousand feet. Why is this name a bit misleading? | Millipedes can only walk on one leg | *Most millipedes have fewer than 400 legs | Millipedes have no legs at all | Millipedes have exactly a thousand legs
exercise: How do you tell a millipede from a centipede? | *Millipedes have two pairs of legs on most body sections, centipedes have one pair | Millipedes live in the sea, centipedes live in trees | Millipedes have one pair of legs per segment, centipedes have two | Millipedes have wings, centipedes do not
test: Where does a millipede live? | *Damp soil and leaf litter | Hot deserts | High on tall mountains | Open ocean
test: What does a millipede do when it is frightened? | *Curls into a tight coil | Flies away | Runs very fast up a wall | Bites hard
exam: Which sentence is true? | *Millipedes eat dead plants and have two pairs of legs on most body sections | Millipedes have one pair of legs per body section | Millipedes are insects with exactly one hundred legs | Arthropleura was a tiny millipede that lived in your garden
